    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="27732c42-d076-50bb-8f4b-4a7f541f13c4" activityNameId="3f0105f8-87c5-5664-b436-6f81d7f33ebd" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Disposal, sewer system, cast iron pipe, DN 800, profile 1</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Disposal, sewer system, cast iron pipe, DN 800, profile 1
Modern Swiss und European technologies are applied to building machines, material production and building processes. 
UUID: 01b6091a-6031-4d9a-91a5-700a625db5e5
This process models deconstruction and end-of-life treatment for 1 meter of installed sewer infrastructure with cast iron pipe. DN 800, profile 1 according to SIA 190. Trench depth: 3 meters. This process includes the deconstruction phase (C1), transport phase (C2), treatment/ recycling phase (C3), and final disposal phase (C4) for 1 meter of sewer system with cast iron pipe, DN 300, profile 1. The operation of similar types of building machines across different processes is aggregated to one process.
Location: Switzerland
Technology: DN 800, profile 1 according to SIA 190.Trench depth 3 meters. Cast iron pipe, ID 800 mm, outer diameter 831 mm, wall thickness 15.6 mm, 287 kg/m, 7200 kg/m³ 
Time period: Review of data currency scheduled after 5 years.
Production volume: 
Sampling: 
Extrapolations: None
Uncertainty adjustments: None
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_01b6091a-6031-4d9a-91a5-700a625db5e5.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
